# This project is built from Windows (ESP-IDF, idf.py) and from WSL (the SDL2
# simulator, the unit tests) against the same working tree, and core.autocrlf is
# true on the Windows side. Without this, tools/idf.sh is checked out with CRLF
# and WSL refuses to run it: "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
#
# So: normalise text to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one thing that wants CRLF; cmd.exe is not reliable without
# it once a file grows labels or multi-line blocks.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let line-ending conversion near these.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
